@startuml Login With Google Sequence Diagram
title UC03 - Login With Google

actor "User" as User
boundary "Login Page" as Frontend
participant ":authRoutes" as Routes
participant ":authController" as Controller
participant ":authService" as Service
participant ":GoogleOAuth" as GoogleOAuth
participant ":User Model" as UserModel
database ":MongoDB" as DB

activate User
User -> Frontend: 1. Click "Sign in with Google"
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Frontend: 2. Open Google OAuth popup

Frontend -> GoogleOAuth: 3. Redirect to Google
activate GoogleOAuth

User -> GoogleOAuth: 4. Enter credentials and consent

GoogleOAuth --> Frontend: 5. Return OAuth Token
deactivate GoogleOAuth

opt [Invalid Token]
    Frontend --> User: 5.1 Display error
end

Frontend -> Routes: 6. POST /api/auth/google/callback?token\n(Bearer Token)
activate Routes

Routes -> Controller: 7. googleLogin(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: 8. googleLogin(token)
activate Service

Service -> GoogleOAuth: 9. verifyToken(token)
activate GoogleOAuth

opt [Token invalid]
    GoogleOAuth --> Service: 9.1 Error
    
    Service --> Controller: 9.2 AppError "Invalid Google token" 401
    Controller --> Routes: 9.3 HTTP 401 Response
    Routes --> Frontend: 9.4 JSON Error
    Frontend --> User: 9.5 Display error
end

GoogleOAuth --> Service: 10. Return user info (email, name, picture)
deactivate GoogleOAuth

Service -> UserModel: 11. findOne({email})
activate UserModel

UserModel -> DB: 12. Query user by email
activate DB

DB --> UserModel: 13. User document or null
deactivate DB

UserModel --> Service: 14. User data
deactivate UserModel

opt [User not exists]
    Service -> Service: 14.1 Validate email domain
    Service -> UserModel: 14.2 create({email, name, avatar, provider: "google"})
    activate UserModel
    UserModel -> DB: 14.3 Insert new user
    activate DB
    DB --> UserModel: 14.4 Created user
    deactivate DB
    UserModel --> Service: 15.5 User data
    deactivate UserModel
end

Service -> Service: 15. Generate JWT token

Service --> Controller: 16. Return {user, token}
deactivate Service

Controller --> Routes: 17. HTTP 200 Response
deactivate Controller

Routes --> Frontend: 18. JSON {user, token}
deactivate Routes

Frontend -> Frontend: 19. Save token to localStorage

Frontend --> User: 20. Redirect to home page
deactivate Frontend
deactivate User
@enduml
